          "evidence": "ServiceTitan's 10-Q (FY2026) states: 'Increased customer adoption of ServiceTitan's platform leads to further data and insights, allowing the company to build more differentiated features and address opportunities in new trades, use cases and customer subsegments.' The company's Titan Intelligence AI engine is powered by years of FSM operational data from thousands of trades businesses, and Atlas (launched Sept 2025) applies this at the dispatch, reporting, and marketing automation layer. The dataset is proprietary and would take a competitor 2-3 years of equivalent scale to replicate — but the advantage is 'moderate' rather than 'strong' because competitors (Jobber, HCP) are building their own AI layers, and AI model quality is not purely data-volume dependent at the SMB FSM use-case level.",
          "evidence_source": "researched",
          "source": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001638826/000163882626000094/ttan-20260731.htm",
          "trajectory": "building"
        },
        {
          "id": "switching_costs",
          "status": "strong",
          "evidence": "ServiceTitan has the deepest switching cost profile in the FSM category. Implementation investment ranges from $5,000 to $50,000+ upfront, creating sunk cost that makes abandonment painful. Annual contracts are mandatory. The platform integrates deeply with QuickBooks, financing platforms, supplier networks, and payroll systems. Years of job history, customer records, and performance data live in the platform in non-portable formats. Teams are trained on ServiceTitan workflows and certified through its partner ecosystem. A switch would require data migration, retraining, system reconnection, and typically months of parallel operation — a real barrier even when an alternative is objectively better.",
          "evidence_source": "agent_estimate",
          "trajectory": "stable"
        },
