          "evidence_source": "agent_estimate",
          "trajectory": "building"
        },
        {
          "id": "switching_costs",
          "status": "moderate",
          "evidence": "Jobber accumulates customer job histories, quotes, invoices, and communication records within the platform. Its 100+ app integrations (Stripe, Zapier, Mailchimp, The Home Depot, GPS tracking) create integration surface area that takes effort to replicate elsewhere. Annual billing plans lock customers in for 12 months; mid-term cancellation means paying through term end. Per-plan user caps escalate costs as teams grow, creating a form of pricing-based stickiness. Data is exportable and migration is feasible in weeks, not months — hence moderate rather than strong.",
